# w.lang.en: what is known about English grammar, as facts, for any application that reads English. Closed word
# classes (determiners, pronouns, prepositions, small numbers), morphology, clause structure, ellipsis markers, the
# grammar as plain productions over categories with the English constructions they belong to, the argument frames of
# the acts of k.actions, and phrase groups. Open-class words are not here: nouns and adjectives are k.words, verbs
# k.actions, number words and colours k.values. A parser that applies this world is the library's std.grammar
# (soplang-words-lib); a category is read from the facts of the type its `w.lang.en.cat` names (`type=`).
# sources: psys2 78f45863 (PSys2 handover/lang.en, the demo's English as facts; CC0); psys2 447a5f9a (PSys2
#   src/lang/en.local.mjs: frames and joiners written after the import, in this world's format; CC0); hand-core 1 (what this
#   repository added: the types of parts, constructions, categories and words, and the slot lines)
# license: CC0-1.0
# script: none (hand-written); the shards are written by tools/import/psys2-lang-en.mjs, except shards/hand-*.sop

@w.lang.en core.module name=w.lang.en version=5 exports=det exports=pron exports=anaphor exports=prep exports=prep.time exports=number exports=ordinal exports=numeral exports=inflect exports=irregular exports=noun.exception exports=contraction exports=contraction.ending exports=cat exports=word exports=rule exports=construction exports=frame exports=part exports=fixed exports=phrase exports=lex exports=joiner exports=joiner.keep exports=frame_lead exports=correction exports=correction.lead exports=answer exports=wh exports=aux exports=neg exports=neg.imperative exports=neg.imperative.skip exports=imperative.lead exports=ellipsis.lead exports=ellipsis.trail exports=ellipsis.repeat exports=ellipsis.starter exports=ellipsis.param exports=coord.sep exports=coord.param exports=relpron exports=copula exports=partitive exports=other exports=choice exports=role_map exports=mode_map exports=template exports=phrasing exports=discourse exports=slot exports=onset exports=alternation exports=alternation_family exports=alternation_case exports=variant exports=skip exports=closed exports=class exports=ending exports=irregular_form exports=arrangement exports=calc exports=reply exports=fn exports=feeling_reply exports=count exports=cue core.source="psys2 78f45863"

# ---- closed word classes ----
# A determiner or quantifier. `in` names a view: one of the lists PSys2 kept in its modules (acts, expand, dialogue,
# discourse, routing); the views differ by accident and are kept until an application unifies them.
