# The class of a closed-class word (reviewer block "02:15", for type signatures): one fact per word and class, derived
# from the word lists above and below (`from`: the lists the word is in; the lists stay the home of the words) by the
# tables of tools/lang-en-closed.mjs (shard closed-classes, rerun by the build). The classes are the closed parts of
# speech of Universal Dependencies in English words: determiner DET, pronoun PRON, preposition ADP, conjunction
# CCONJ/SCONJ, auxiliary AUX, numeral NUM, ordinal (ADJ, NumType=Ord), adverb ADV (the function adverbs of the
# lists), particle PART, interjection INTJ. Multi-word entries of a one-class list are one word of it ("in front of",
# "how many"); phrases of the marker lists ("scratch that") and open-class words in them (want, think) have none.
@w.lang.en.closed core.type of=w.lang.en.closed shared=true closed=true core.source="hand-core 1"
@w.lang.en.closed.text core.slot of=w.lang.en.closed key=text id=true required=true kind=atom kind=string core.source="hand-core 1"
@w.lang.en.closed.class core.slot of=w.lang.en.closed key=class id=true required=true enum=determiner enum=pronoun enum=preposition enum=conjunction enum=auxiliary enum=numeral enum=ordinal enum=adverb enum=particle enum=interjection core.source="hand-core 1"
@w.lang.en.closed.from core.slot of=w.lang.en.closed key=from many=true required=true kind=atom core.source="hand-core 1"

# A phrase that says how things are arranged (block "04:40" item 4: "in a circle", "evenly", "left to right", "top to
# bottom"): `layout` the arrangement of k.layouts it names (ring, grid, row, column ...), `relation` the k.layouts
# relation it asks between the things (evenly_spaced, left_of, above, inside, apart), `inverse=yes` when it says that
# relation the other way round (right to left), `direction` the order it reads the things in, `diagram_layout` the
# layout of a w.diagram it asks for (circular, grid, left_right, top_down, radial, overlapping, free). Hand-written
# (shard hand-arrangements); a test keeps every value a value of k.layouts and w.diagram.
@w.lang.en.arrangement core.type of=w.lang.en.arrangement shared=true closed=true core.source="hand-core 1"
@w.lang.en.arrangement.text core.slot of=w.lang.en.arrangement key=text id=true required=true kind=atom kind=string core.source="hand-core 1"
@w.lang.en.arrangement.layout core.slot of=w.lang.en.arrangement key=layout kind=atom kind=string type=k.layouts.layout by=name core.source="hand-core 1"
@w.lang.en.arrangement.relation core.slot of=w.lang.en.arrangement key=relation enum=left_of enum=above enum=inside enum=around enum=on enum=beside enum=evenly_spaced enum=apart enum=aligned_row enum=aligned_column core.source="hand-core 1"
@w.lang.en.arrangement.inverse core.slot of=w.lang.en.arrangement key=inverse enum=yes core.source="hand-core 1"
@w.lang.en.arrangement.direction core.slot of=w.lang.en.arrangement key=direction enum=left_to_right enum=right_to_left enum=top_to_bottom enum=bottom_to_top enum=clockwise enum=anticlockwise core.source="hand-core 1"
@w.lang.en.arrangement.diagram_layout core.slot of=w.lang.en.arrangement key=diagram_layout enum=top_down enum=left_right enum=radial enum=circular enum=grid enum=overlapping enum=free core.source="hand-core 1"

# Arithmetic words (reviewer 09:20, PSys2 Q18 K4; shard arithmetic, tools/lang-en-arithmetic.mjs): a word or phrase of
# arithmetic, its `kind` (operator, comparison, aggregate, extreme, state), how it is said (`form`: infix "3 plus 4",
# prefix "double 6", split "share 12 between 3" with its `marker` words, relation "3 more than Tom", question "how many
# more"), the core.calc function it names (`calc`: the builtins add, sub, mul, div, eq, sum, argmax, argmin), a
# `factor` for a word that multiplies by a fixed number (double 2, half 0.5), the `state` of a story's quantity a state
# word asks for (left and now: now; at first: start), and an example.
@w.lang.en.calc core.type of=w.lang.en.calc shared=true closed=true core.source="hand-core 1"
